<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Lugal-zage-si</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">r. c. 2358–2334 BCE</span> · <a href="/centuries/24th-century-bce">24th century BCE</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Lugal-zage-si was a Sumerian king of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/umma">Umma</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/uruk">Uruk</a> who brought much of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sumer">Sumer</a> under his rule in the twenty-fourth century BCE. He was defeated and captured by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sargon-of-akkad">Sargon of Akkad</a>. His defeat made Sargon master of southern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mesopotamia">Mesopotamia</a> and was a key step in founding the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/akkadian-empire">Akkadian Empire</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/lugal-zage-si.jpg" alt="Lugal-zage-si" width="317" height="420" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: ALFGRN · CC BY-SA 2.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Prisoner_exiting_a_cage,_on_an_Akkadian_Empire_victory_stele_circa_2300_BCE,_Louvre_Museum.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
